# DOC-sprint: SPRINT.oot as living execution board

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| **Paper ID** | `DOC-sprint` |
| **Subject document(s)** | monorepo `SPRINT.oot` |
| **Status** | `draft` |
| **Series** | Documentation system (`DOC-*`) |

## 1. Why this document exists

SPRINT.oot is the high-churn execution board: tip SHA, rebuild defaults, agent safety, M1–M7 gate/depth, residuals, rails. It answers what we are doing this cycle.

## 2. Problem statement

Without a living board, multi-agent work thrashs, tip pins rot, and residual honesty is forgotten mid-feature. PM is too large for one turn (TOOLS power law ≤5).

## 3. Related work (university + commercial)

- Scrum Sprint Backlog — visible plan for the current sprint. https://scrumguides.org/scrum-guide.html
- Product vs sprint backlog. https://www.atlassian.com/agile/scrum/backlogs
- Kanban WIP limits — related to Little’s law in TOOLS.

## 4. Rationale for openOODA

Tip SHA for agents; M-table for gate vs depth honesty; residuals for fail-closed memory; machine safety; rails block. Must not redefine DESIGN.

## 5. Limits and failure modes

Stale if not updated each depth push. Not residual deep docs. Monorepo may lack remote.

## 6. Alternatives considered

Wiki-only, issue-tracker-only, single mega-README, or oral tradition — all fail multi-agent continuity or honesty. Prefer git-versioned markdown with clear roles.

## 7. Reality (honesty)

Used heavily in 2026-08 depth work; linked from TOOLS and site.

## 8. Open questions

1. Mirror SPRINT into ooda/bootstrap for GH-only readers?
2. Auto-close lines when CI green?

## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Tip SHA on each depth push.
- [ ] Residuals match residual docs.

